1
00:00:08,930 --> 00:00:10,430
I had an interview today, too.

2
00:00:10,430 --> 00:00:11,780
I had a great interview

3
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:14,230
with Admissions at Columbia University.

4
00:00:14,230 --> 00:00:15,160
Really?

5
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,410
What did they say?

6
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:17,850
Will you get into the school?

7
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:19,880
Well, they didn't say anything for sure.

8
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:23,680
But I figure that with my grades and with my personality,

9
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:25,480
I'll have no problem.

10
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:27,790
Columbia's a terrific school.

11
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:29,120
What are you going to do?

12
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:31,470
Do? I don't know.

13
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:34,210
I also applied to NYU.

14
00:00:34,210 --> 00:00:36,520
You sound excited about Columbia.

15
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,430
What's your problem, Mike?

16
00:00:38,430 --> 00:00:41,050
Indecision. Indecision.

17
00:00:41,050 --> 00:00:41,860
It's not easy,

18
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:44,210
and this is an important decision we have to make.

19
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:45,460
What about you?

20
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,360
How was your interview with Michigan?

21
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:48,970
The interview was fine.

22
00:00:48,970 --> 00:00:50,900
It's a great college.

23
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:52,170
It is.

24
00:00:52,170 --> 00:00:54,110
My father would like me to go there.

25
00:00:54,110 --> 00:00:56,570
He and my Grandpa both went there.

26
00:00:56,570 --> 00:00:58,250
Great medical school, too.

27
00:00:58,250 --> 00:01:00,260
I know.

28
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:02,410
You can follow in your father's footsteps.

29
00:01:02,410 --> 00:01:06,490
Ah! I'd like to follow in my own footsteps, Mike.

30
00:01:06,490 --> 00:01:08,260
What do you want to study?

31
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:09,970
I've been thinking.

32
00:01:09,970 --> 00:01:12,290
I think I want to study journalism

33
00:01:12,290 --> 00:01:14,580
to be a reporter--a newspaperman.

34
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:17,870
You do a pretty good job on the Riverdale High School paper.

35
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:20,340
And I've been thinking about it a lot lately.

36
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:22,400
Have you discussed it with your parents?

37
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:25,420
No. But I have to.

38
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:37,240
OK. Let's talk.

39
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:41,930
Hi, Son. Is everything all right?

40
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:44,890
Hi, Dad. Everything's fine.

41
00:01:44,890 --> 00:01:46,640
I was just waiting for you to get home

42
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:47,710
so we could talk.

43
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:50,520
Anything special you want to talk about?

44
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:53,190
There is, Dad.

45
00:01:53,190 --> 00:01:55,290
I'm listening.

46
00:01:55,290 --> 00:01:59,490
Well, I know you and Mom have given up a lot

47
00:01:59,490 --> 00:02:02,730
to save money for my college tuition.

48
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:04,310
We want you to go to college, Robbie.

49
00:02:04,310 --> 00:02:06,800
I know. I do.

50
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,790
But?

51
00:02:08,790 --> 00:02:13,380
Well, I've thought a lot about which college,

52
00:02:13,380 --> 00:02:16,210
and one of them is Columbia.

53
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:20,510
Columbia? Why Columbia?

54
00:02:20,510 --> 00:02:25,690
First, they have an excellent School of Journalism.

55
00:02:25,690 --> 00:02:27,910
They do.

56
00:02:27,910 --> 00:02:32,180
And your friends are planning to go to Columbia?

57
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:34,440
That's only part of it.

58
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:38,040
It's complicated.

59
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:40,140
I'll try to explain.

60
00:02:40,140 --> 00:02:43,790
Mike and I had a hamburger this afternoon, and we talked.

61
00:02:43,790 --> 00:02:45,530
Yes?

62
00:02:45,530 --> 00:02:48,440
Well, we talked about a lot of things.

63
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:49,780
He applied to Columbia,

64
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:51,860
and his interview was very successful.

65
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:53,230
He thinks he'll be accepted,

66
00:02:53,230 --> 00:02:56,760
and he really wants to go there.

67
00:02:56,760 --> 00:03:00,040
Dean Rafer called me today.

68
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:04,060
He told me he was very impressed with you.

69
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:05,390
He's a nice man.

70
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:07,920
He was very kind.

71
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:09,850
He told me

72
00:03:09,850 --> 00:03:13,620
you had some doubts about wanting to go to Michigan.

73
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:15,950
Yes. I do.

74
00:03:15,950 --> 00:03:20,090
I'm just not sure about what I want to do.

75
00:03:20,090 --> 00:03:23,140
That's OK.

76
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:25,380
You understand?

77
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:28,110
Let me tell you something, Robbie.

78
00:03:28,110 --> 00:03:34,880
Something that might be surprising to you.

79
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:39,480
What? Tell me.

80
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:46,600
Well, Grandpa wanted me to study engineering, like him.

81
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:49,490
Well, I wasn't clear about my future,

82
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:55,910
but I knew engineering was not for me.

83
00:03:55,910 --> 00:03:59,250
What did you tell Grandpa?

84
00:03:59,250 --> 00:04:02,840
The truth.

85
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,230
Then you're not upset

86
00:04:04,230 --> 00:04:08,300
about my not wanting to go into medicine?

87
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:10,720
I'm not upset at all.

88
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:14,970
I'm just happy that we're able to talk about it.

89
00:04:14,970 --> 00:04:18,260
I am too, Dad.

90
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:22,580
I suppose you want to apply to Columbia.

91
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:28,820
Yes, but I also want to apply to several other colleges.

92
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:30,570
I thought you wanted to go to Columbia.

93
00:04:30,570 --> 00:04:32,950
Well, I might want to go to Columbia.

94
00:04:32,950 --> 00:04:35,300
But I might not.

95
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:39,600
I just want to be able to make my own decision.

96
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:42,740
You're a real Stewart!

97
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:47,130
And if I think about it long enough, you never know ...

98
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:48,650
Never know what?

99
00:04:48,650 --> 00:04:51,850
If I make my own decision,

100
00:04:51,850 --> 00:04:57,050
I might choose Michigan.

101
00:04:57,050 --> 00:04:59,180
Robbie, you're something!

102
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:02,730
You know, when I was your age,

103
00:05:02,730 --> 00:05:05,730
I said exactly the same thing to Grandpa.
